{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he said:</b> The sense is: HaShem did not give me wealth, but I enriched myself on my own. For it is not like כנען; it is the merchant, like לא יהיה עוד כנעני, and the sense is: why should he say kindness and justice preserve, and not oppression like a Canaanite. And all my toil — people will not find that I have sinned."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The comment addresses Hosea 12:8–9. The biblical text reads כנען with a final alef, which Ibn Ezra glosses as 'merchant.' The negative in the last clause (לא ימצאו) may apply to the people or to the toil; rendered hyper-literally to preserve the ambiguity."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:02.064659809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}